Robert,

To make the MFN clause meaningful (rather than ornamental), we need
all four pillars below. Anything less and Orion can technically
charge another customer a lower per-user fee with impunity:

  1. **MFN guarantee** — per-user fee shall not exceed lowest offered
     to "substantially similar" customers.
  2. **Certification** — quarterly CFO-signed certificate of
     compliance.
  3. **Retroactive true-up** — refund of difference if a lower fee
     was offered, with 30-day cure window.
  4. **Audit right** — once per year, confidential.

Suggested draft language attached separately. Will share with
Orion's counsel today.

— Aisha

