Robert,

Following our discussion last week, Orion is open to including a
most-favored-nation pricing clause in the upcoming license amendment.

I'd like to keep the language tight — typically MFN clauses describe
intent only, not enforcement mechanics. Our preferred shape is a
one-line statement that Orion will not charge other customers lower
per-user fees for "substantially similar" usage.

Let me know if your counsel can work with that shape.

— Deepa
